  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Time of the Season** (2 reviews): Identified as a cover of the Association song; Written by Rod Argent, who performed it with the Zombies [2][5]\n- **Picture of You** (1 review): Listener reports getting chills while listening to this specific track [4]\n- **O Is The One That Is Real** (1 review): Identified as a track from the Split EP with Ohia [2]\n- **It's About Twilight Now** (1 review): Identified as a song by the band Tennessee Fire [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Old September Blues**: back after 22 archived shows (558 days) [6]\n- **By My Car**: rare: 13 archived performances [6]\n- **Time of the Season**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2003-09-27.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 23 songs; 139 min; rated 4.75/5 by 4 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer describes the recording's sound quality as superb; Listener rates the audio quality of the tape as excellent [3][4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2003-09-27.shnf**: taped by Jon Ice; transferred by Jon Ice; source: AKG ck63 > Active Cables > JK LABS DVC > Canare Starquad Interconnects > Apogee Mini Me (line in) > Powerbook @ 24 bit/48k [1]",
